  "component_cases": [
    {
      "case_id": "u6-req-0091",
      "algorithms": [
        "EdDSA",
        "ES256"
      ],
      "test": "auxiliary_clauses::production_cancellation_observations_correlate_each_physical_invitation_and_keep_the_durable_boundary",
      "assertions": [
        "Two authenticated physical peers sharing an Identity, credential and Device receive distinct signed forwarded invitation IDs, then each receives its own signed session.cancel with in_reply_to equal to that exact ID.",
        "Native and HTTP ordinary cancellations each cause the bounded recipient observation. The original source correlation, CID/SID, inviter by, code487 and request-cancelled text are exact; no connid is invented.",
        "Logical cancellation replay returns the same durable receipt without repeating the mutation or creating another invitation worker. A bounded final read observes no duplicate notification.",
        "A late signed accept cannot revive the cancelled Session; its current recipient snapshot remains cancelled at topology revision1."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "Schema91 freezes only still-pending targets of their latest original invitation source in the ordinary cancellation transaction. Original by/epoch/reason/time facts are immutable and independent of later record finalization.",
    "A dedicated exact current PeerCommand cancellation-read union rechecks credential/Device/key, original/current source audience, current inviter/target epochs and recipient ceiling through actual reliable IO. Binding-only proofs and revoked named read authority refuse.",
    "The protected route API exposes the final signed request ID before awaiting a decision; the bounded waiter retains metadata only. Cancellation is checked on journal wake and a100ms recovery tick. The write is one bounded hint attempt, never a repeated mutation.",
    "Already rejected targets get no cancellation fact. A storage fault rolls back all cancellation effects, and retry of the same logical command recovers the original facts."
  ],
